[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Indian Defense, Accelerated London System, vs fianchetto"]
[ECO "A45"]
[Character "solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "h3-bishop-retreat,queenside-space"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. Bf4 g6
(2... e6 3. e3 d5 4. Nd2)
3. e3 3... Bg7
4. Nf3 4... O-O
5. Be2 { Against a fianchetto the bishop belongs on e2: it covers the kingside and leaves d3 for a pawn if needed. } 5... d6
6. h3 { Gives the bishop on f4 the retreat square h2, so ...Nh5 or ...e5 cannot trap it. } 6... Nbd7
(6... c5 7. c3)
7. O-O 7... b6
8. Bh2 { Out of the way of ...e5 and ...Nh5, and it still watches the long diagonal toward Black's king. } 8... Bb7
9. a4 { Stops ...b5 and gains space on the queenside. } 9... a6
10. c3 { Supports d4 and makes room for Nbd2 and Qc2. With the centre solid, Black has no way to open it favourably. Plan: Nbd2, Qc2 and e4. } *
